../../INSTRUCTION.md:7:- **Fan-out:** each item's build + Codex wave is an independent agent task — the cycle spawns one subagent per item with the item's full §1–§5 charge; the seat coordinates, verifies each item's filings firsthand (scores.md arithmetic, purity of the filed build), and closes the cycle record. T15's attempt is the measured unit: one bounded build + four Codex runs, not a 6-hour job.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:9:- Artifact directory per item: `hidden_files/study/recreations/<technique-id>-<slug>/` — created at Plan, holds segment cut + recreation.html + comparison.html + scores.md + codex/ returns.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:13:- **Completion-wave form (Amendment A8, 2026-11-16, Cycle 021 Condense — re-encoded under codex-condense REVISE before landing):** a wave whose predecessor stopped mid-Execute/Verify is completed by the next cycle: the completing cycle's §1 prices each unfinished item's on-disk state (artifact census + which prescribed calls already fired), and before any standing payload is fired its hash binding to the filed build is verified. Completion items occupy wave slots and count toward the §0 cap; new items fill only the remaining slots. The completing cycle restates per item the standing guidance dispositions and mechanics citations the item's Plan binds to (a prior cycle's §2b is evidence, not working memory), and carries each mid-attempt item to its verdict on the filed builds: hash-bound payloads and filed gate returns are consumed, never silently re-fired or rebuilt; where an item's record layer is missing (no build-record, no A6 legs, no gate filings), the completing cycle authors it from cited sources — the filed build plus the predecessor cycle's §§1b/2/2b — with the sources printed on the authored record's face and no fact claimed from builder memory, then fires the missing prescribed calls. First demonstration: Cycle 021 Wave 18 (2026-11-16) — T123 payloads consumed · T124 prewave consumed · T129 record authored from filed build + Cycle-020 §§1b/2/2b · T130 taken in the remaining slot.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:22:- **RESOURCE LIST (read in this order, every wave):** (1) `../QUEUE.md` recreation-queue section — current positions, OWED status, ownership split (first attempts here; scored techniques route to practice) · (2) the item's packet section in its digest.md + TECHNIQUES.md entry (style-library) · (3) the item's prior scores.md + codex/ returns + `verdict-history.md` lines, including named family siblings (e.g. T16 reads T15's filings) · (4) the evidence frames + archived source segment in motion · (5) this file's Amendments A1/A3/A5 guidance for the item's family (flow-field model + Owner Cures 1–2 for particle fields; runtime text sampling for typography) · (6) `guards/guards.md` command list.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:24:- **Observe-exit call:** `guards/jev-observe-exit.md` fires at this gate on every cycle and judges the gate-out block per item before §2 opens for that item. The phase advances on the verdict's recorded disposition (applied, or set aside with reason; applied gaps are carried into §2 as named charges). An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:26:## §2 — Plan
../../INSTRUCTION.md:29:3. **Bar pricing (standing, priced at founding 2026-11-13):** consolidation requires Codex wave average ≥85 AND no lens under 70. Priced judgment: the average alone would let a fatal lens (purity at 40) hide inside three good scores; the per-lens floor is what makes the bar a proof rather than a vibe, and 85 is high enough that a PASS means production can lift the machinery without re-deriving it. The bar stands as charged unless a scored cycle produces evidence against it — then the evidence goes to HQ, the bar does not move silently.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:30:4. **Verification plan:** swap test design (which config values change — at minimum the words; plus one timing and one palette value), purity checks (§6.1 greps + asset inventory), comparison sync method, and the Codex wave composition (four lenses, §5).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:32:- **Plan's standing product:** the Execute checklist (§3 steps as an itemized list) AND the Verify checklist (each deliverable property with its checking instrument — swap-test altered values, purity grep patterns, comparison check, jev-prewave call point, five-lens wave composition) AND the failure-point evaluation (per item, priced from this job's record: convergent freeze · intensity collapse · phrase overlap · fitting limits · render-proof limitation), all in RUN.md at this gate.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:33:- **Plan-exit call:** `guards/jev-plan-exit.md` fires at this gate on every cycle and judges the Plan product per item (parameter table · checklists · failure points · plateau priced in Plan per Amendment A2 — prior/family average + the stuck-lens hypothesis stated before Execute, not discovered at close) before §3 opens. `guards/codex-plan-review.md` fires alongside it for every item. Both verdicts are advisory: the phase advances on their recorded dispositions (applied, or set aside with reason). An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:36:1. **Cut the original segment** from the archived source at the catalogue timestamps (±0.5 s handles) into the artifact directory as `segment.mp4`, re-encoded for browser playback. The segment is EVIDENCE: it appears in the comparison labeled ORIGINAL, and nowhere else. Bulk media stays local (sync pointer rule).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:38:3. **Build `comparison.html`** — the deliverable's face: original segment and live recreation side by side at matched size, ONE synchronized control set (play/pause/restart drives both; the recreation's clock slaved to the video's currentTime or to a shared start timestamp), each side labeled (ORIGINAL — <specimen> @ <timestamps> · RECREATION — <technique>, parameterized). On a phone-width screen the two stack vertically with the controls still reachable (fleet tappability law).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:39:4. **Self-verify before Codex** (§5 legs 1–3); a build that fails its own swap test does not spend a Codex wave. Self-verify files the A12 executable receipts (§5 leg 3b) in the build-record's first draft; a build-record missing receipts does not spend the prewave call either.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:40:Gate out: segment + recreation + comparison on disk; self-verify recorded.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:41:- Execute follows the Plan's Execute checklist and fires the Verify guards named in the Plan's Verify checklist — no step is improvised past the checklist; a step the checklist cannot cover returns the item to §2 (REVISE), it is not invented in Execute.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:45:## §5 — Verify (the Codex scoring wave + own checks)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:47:2. **Construction purity (own, mechanical):** grep the recreation for the original's media (segment filename, source filename, frame-sequence patterns, <video>/<img> pointing at specimen media) — any hit is a refusal-class defect (§6.1). Asset inventory: every asset the recreation loads is listed and is either code or generated/created by this build.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:50:4. **Codex scoring wave (external):** FIVE reviewers, distinct lenses — **motion fidelity · timing/tempo match · construction purity · reusability/parameterization · readability** (the fifth lens is permanent since 2026-11-14, Amendment A5: formed-word legibility against the particle field — word-vs-reserve intensity separation present and sufficient · the word readable at phone size during its hold · background particles never competing at word intensity). Each run: instruction file opens with the standing header (consumer + the decision the run prices; the working record it builds from and writes to; the return must name what it wrote into the body), carries the technique's catalogue mechanics + the recreation's full source, and returns ONE lens score (0–100) + priced findings. Feeding follows the fleet's Codex rule (instructions + artifact in ONE stream; never pipe + stdin field together). Returns are filed verbatim under the artifact's `codex/` directory.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:54:## §6 — Guards (standing, every cycle)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:55:1. **Construction purity (refusal-class):** the recreation is HTML/CSS/JS + generated/created assets only. Embedding the original video, a frame sequence of it, or a traced redraw of a frame as the "recreation" is a refusal-class defect — the cycle stops, the defect is recorded, the build is discarded. The original appears ONLY as the labeled comparison side.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:59:5. **No captions/subtitles** in recreation or comparison (fleet law); technique text is subject, not caption.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:68:## Amendment A1 (2026-11-13, from Cycle-002 — T15 attempt 1)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:69:1. **Convergent-lens rule (§5 reading rule):** when two or more lenses independently name the same defect, that defect is priced as the next attempt's primary cure, ahead of single-lens findings. (T15 attempt 1: motion 68 + reuse 64 both named the surplus-particle freeze during FORM.)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:70:2. **Typography construction precedent:** runtime sampling of config-rendered text is the lawful letterform construction (purity 100, T15 attempt 1) — future typography recreations start from it rather than re-deriving purity.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:72:## Amendment A2 (2026-11-13, the funnel design — score-delta floor rule, HQ's priced addition)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:80:## Amendment A5 (2026-11-14, the owner's own read on T15 attempt 1 — two cures + the fifth lens)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:84:3. **THE FIFTH LENS — READABILITY (permanent, §5.4):** the founding evidence is priced: four lenses scored a recreation whose words fight their own background, and none owned legibility. The owner's expectation now has a judge (the golden rule). Attempt 2 onward is scored by five lenses; the bar form is unchanged (average ≥85, no lens <70) with the fifth lens inside both terms. Attempts scored under the four-lens wave keep their filed averages — cross-wave comparisons print the lens count (a 4-lens 78.5 and a 5-lens score are different instruments; deltas across the boundary are labeled as such).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:88:Read the run's traces + Codex returns → candidate lessons (which constructions scored well on which lenses; recurring Codex findings across techniques) → label demonstrated/candidate/planned → promote into this file (dated, technique cited) + verdict-history.md → next cycle inherits. A lens finding that recurs across two techniques is a pattern: it becomes a §6 guard candidate with the two citations.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:110:2. **Gate-order sequencing (A9.2).** No build script is written before the Observe-exit and Plan-exit returns are filed and consumed in the wave's §2b. A draft produced earlier is a deviation printed in §2b, never silently rebuilt over.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:111:3. **Count assertion (A9.3).** Every table-driven build prints source-count vs built-count and halts on mismatch — in the item's build-record (builder side) AND in the wave record's own summary lines (seat side): a summary count in a gate or Verify section is machine-counted against the table it summarizes before that section closes, and a mismatch blocks the section's closure until the record carries the corrected count with its source note. (Founding catches: T134's truncated sentence table, Cycle 022 · the §2b 33-vs-37 summary in Cycle 023, caught builder-side before this landing.)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:112:4. **Raw-output filing (A9.4).** Build-records file the raw harness output (swap test, purity grep, syntax check) from the first draft, not a summary of it; a build-record whose own-checks section carries claims without the raw output beneath them is an ASSERTED-CHECKS defect at jev-prewave.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:113:5. **Gate-out reasoning inline (A9.5).** A gate-out section carries its dispositions' reasoning inline — the construction-precedent dispositions (A1 §2's scope, A5's applicability) are stated with their reasoning in the Observe gate-out itself, not only in a later Plan section the gate judge is not fed. (Founding miss: Cycle 023's jev-observe-exit GUIDANCE-DROPPED return — the reasoning stood in §2 while the judged record was §1.)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:118:1. **Prewave payload completeness (A10.1 — restates §5 leg 3b at instruction level; operative since Cycle 024 in jev-prewave.md's context contract).** The jev-prewave payload for every item MUST carry that item's A6 leg outputs (fit-table.md + config-census.md) verbatim. A payload lacking either leg's output is a feeder defect printed in the wave's §5; a prewave verdict priced without them does not discharge leg 3b.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:123:Every item maps each Observe census checkpoint to an executable own-check assertion and its CONFIG-derived evaluation instant. The build-record identifies the checkpoint, the assertion, the CONFIG expression, and the evaluated result. jev-prewave returns ASSERTED-CHECKS if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent. A CONFIG timing swap must move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Demonstrations: practice T153 (timing 45→92) + T162 (timing 64→96), practice Cycle 019 · recreation Wave 25, all four items (timing lenses 92/96/96/100, no timing-stuck item, against Wave 22's allocation-vs-census timing failures at 68/64). Enforcement lives in jev-prewave.md §2 leg (3), amended in the same landing.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:126:1. **Receipt form (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, referenced from §3 step 4).** Every A11 assertion in a build-record files its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT beside the claim — the harness command or run, the CONFIG expression evaluated, and the raw result from the build under review; for a CONFIG timing swap the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant. A9.4 already required raw output; this clause names the receipt's three parts and wires the check into the prewave step itself. A build-record whose assertions carry claims without receipts is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the call's firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, and an unfired call still prints the cycle INCOMPLETE).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:127:2. **Fit evidence form.** In this seat (no browser binary), the lawful fit measurements are (i) harness post-fit ink measurement of the built spans, or (ii) rendered measurement with a named stand-in font — each row printing its instrument, the fitted element + stage geometry, the measured ink bounds, and the margin (guard-measured-fit.md, amended in this same landing: items 1–2 + output form). A character-width × factor MODEL is a HIT under that guard, never a measurement. Demonstrations: T195 (harness post-fit ink measurement → prewave FIRE-WAVE, wave PASS 88.6) · T190 (PIL rendered measurement, named stand-in) · counter-instances T196 + T197 (model rows priced as HITs).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:131:1. **Receipt index + reconciliation (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, extended in the same landing).** Every build-record carries a RECEIPT INDEX enumerating (a) every guards.md command applicable to the item (1 purity · 2 swap · 3 syntax + seeded-RNG census · 4 arithmetic, seat-side · 5 segment binding · 6 fit leg · 7 census leg · 8 census-anchor probes where a zero-state anchor stands) and (b) every A11 assertion for the item. Readiness REQUIRES the reconciliation, not just the index: against the applicable guard commands, the item's planned A11 assertions, and — for a completion or re-attempt — the assertion sets established in the filed prior harnesses and their amendments; census receipts reconcile against the build's expected CONFIG keys (nested/array keys included — founding miss: T190's `scenes[].id` row). Every line carries its executable receipt or an explicit NOT-DEMANDED line whose disposition cites the governing plan or guard; a missing expected line, an unsupported exclusion, or a line with neither is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, per A12.1's form).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:133:3. **Receipt validity (evidence form, not presence).** A receipt is valid only if it carries the evidence its assertion requires: for each CONFIG-derived input, the CONFIG expression and its evaluated value (never a bare number whose CONFIG dependence the judge must take on faith — founding instances: T196's boundary-skip endpoints · T199's census twins); for each check, the raw observed result. Item-specific evidence stands under its own assertion (founding instance: T199's joined CP11 receipt stands under CP11, not as an appendix claim). A populated receipt lacking its required evidence returns the record to the builder under §5 leg 3b's readiness check.
../../guards/guards.md:7:1. Construction-purity grep — recreation.html must contain no reference to source media, frames, or tracing (pattern census over the file).
