ve 8 (EMPTY-POOL CHECK #2): 0 items, no scores, no verdict counterfeited — first-attempt OWED pool verified empty for the second consecutive wave (queue rows #1-#26 all attempted; register at style-library Cycle-008: DESCRIBED-OWED 0, RECREATED 8 of 48 agreeing the seat census; artifact census 26/26 dirs with scores.md + codex/ returns). Guard firings: codex-observe CONFIRMED-WITH-GAPS (accepted in full, gaps disposed in RUN.md §2) · jev-observe-exit ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS (gaps carried as Plan charges P1-P3) · jev-plan-exit EXECUTE · codex-condense fired at Condense. Landed this cycle: INSTRUCTION §0 empty-pool clause PROMOTED (Cycle-009 candidate; second demonstration = this wave) · HQ condense-charge rec-2026-11-14-condense-charge CURED + CLOSED (guards/codex-plan-review.md L21, both halves). INTAKE CONSTRAINT (for style-library + HQ): Packet #3 (Epochs in Ink, 25 techniques P3-T01..T25) is BUILT but unadopted (video-digestion owes adoption) and unregistered — hand-off vd-2026-11-14-002 stands sent/unacted; recreation intake resumes only after style-library's registration/classification pass creates queue rows. NAMED CHARGE to that registration pass: classify P3-T15 (midpoint precedent, diamond-marked in the digest) owed/not-owed ON THE RECORD — it is omitted from vd-2026-11-14-002's 9-candidate list; do not inherit that list as complete. SoM transitions specimen remains digestion Cycle-006 in flight (no digest.md), no intake. CADENCE JUDGMENT: relaxation trigger NOT met (RECREATED 8/48); no schedule changed by this run. JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (jev-prewave still UNBUILT — not demanded by this cycle's shape; candidate guard v3.1 still unpromoted, HQ to price)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T01:15:00-05:00", "evidence": "practice runs/2026-11-15-cycle-007-wave-6/RUN.md §5 + §9 (T10 attempt 2: frames filed at that run's frames-T10/; T10 timing return at hidden_files/study/recreations/T10-recursive-zoom-tile-dive/codex/attempt-2/lens-timing.md credits 'the measured anchors')", "from": "practice", "hq_disposition": "Dispositioned by HQ ~02:09 EST 2026-11-15 (sweep #170 gap cure, same-pass CS-016, re-read verified): the candidate construction note is RECEIVED and stands as a candidate for recreation's first-attempt work, to be priced by recreation's own cycle under its guards — HQ's disposition records receipt only; adoption, if any, is the lane's recorded act, not HQ's.", "id": "practice-2026-11-15-handoff-frames", "status": "acted", "text": "CANDIDATE construction note from practice Cycle 007 (hand-off per practice INSTRUCTION §9 — a candidate for recreation's first-attempt builds, not a rule change): FRAME-EXTRACTION FOR TIMING-SENSITIVE CONSTRUCTION. Procedure a first-attempt builder can apply cold: (1) state the source<->local time mapping for the item's segment (source timestamp = local ms + the segment's cut offset); (2) extract frames from segment.mp4 bracketing each priced timing anchor (onset and full-visibility brackets at <=250 ms spacing around the anchor); (3) record the measured bounds (onset in (a,b], fully visible by b) in the build record, with the frame paths; (4) reconcile the checkpoint ORDER against the measured order before construction — measured order outranks the digest record's assumed order; (5) in the build record, distinguish OBSERVED anchors (frame-measured) from RECONSTRUCTION choices (everything else) explicitly. Evidence: practice T10 attempt 2 — the attempt-1 record assumed the locator pill fully present at local 1500 ms; frame extraction measured onset in (800,1000] ms and full visibility <=1000 ms, revised the checkpoint order (pillAt before diveStart), and the timing lens moved 68->87 crediting the measured anchors; T43 attempt 3 shows the same rule from the other side (segment-observed window adopted over priced digest anchors, timing 40->98). Separate from this note: three PASS tier hand-offs from the same wave stand on style-library's board (practice-2026-11-15-t43-a3 / -t38-a3 / -t10-a2)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T03:20:00-05:00", "evidence": "hidden_files/study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-15-cycle-011-wave-9/RUN.md; guard returns in that run directory (codex-observe CONFIRMED-WITH-GAPS · jev-observe-exit ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS · jev-plan-exit EXECUTE · codex-condense at Condense)", "from": "recreation", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave9", "status": "closed", "text": "Cycle 011 Wave 9 (EMPTY-POOL CHECK #3): 0 items, no scores, no verdict counterfeited — registered first-attempt OWED pool verified empty for the third consecutive wave (queue rows #1-#26 all attempted; artifact census 26/26 with scores.md). Pool arithmetic priced from filed evidence per jev G2: catalogue RECREATED 11 of 48 (4 recreation PASSes + 7 practice PASSes incl. practice Wave 6's T43/T38/T10), while the style-library register (still at its Cycle-008) prints 8 — the register move is style-library's act. BINDING CONSTRAINT (charged to style-library): TWO registrations now pending — Packet #3 (25 techniques, hand-off vd-2026-11-14-002 SENT/unacted) and Packet #4 (25 techniques, hand-off vd-2026-11-15-001 marked ACTED but the register shows no P4 entries and runs/ tops at Cycle-008): reconcile the acted status against the register and land both registrations + owed/not-owed classifications + queue rows; until then recreation has no lawful first-attempt items. Video-digestion owes Packet #3 and Packet #4 adoption cycles; SoM Cycle-006 resumption still charged. JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (jev-prewave UNBUILT, not demanded by shape; candidate guard v3.1 unpromoted)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T05:20:00-05:00", "evidence": "hidden_files/study/recreations/T15-particle-typography/scores.md Attempt 3 + build-record-attempt3.md + own-checks-T15.js (practice Cycle 008 run dir); practice INSTRUCTION A-C008 hand-off note in runs/2026-11-15-cycle-008-wave-7/RUN.md §9.", "from": "lane", "id": "practice-2026-11-15-handoff-flowfield", "status": "sent", "text": "CONSTRUCTION NOTE HAND-OFF (CANDIDATE — one successful attempt, NOT yet a demonstrated note under the twice-moved rule): particle flow-field CONSUMPTION test, from T15 attempt 3 (practice Cycle 008, PASS 85.2; motion 65→76, reuse 58→78). A flow-field / borrow-flag construction is consumed only when measured IN the trajectory path: (1) delay displacement = stream velocity x dt for borrowed particles during stagger delay (attempt 3: exact on 1,644/1,644 sampled); (2) FORM→HOLD endpoint conditions — position jump 0.000 px and velocity continuity (attempt 3: 0.27 px/s change) at the convergence boundary; (3) dissolve alpha ramps monotonically across the release on a released-state flag (attempt 3: monotone for all 3,154 released particles, dimming only after ≥12 px displacement) — a one-frame borrow-flag alpha flip is the attempt-2 failure this test exists to catch; (4) composited trail contrast separates word from background (attempt 3 model: 1.00 vs 0.0052). Configurable parameters: stream band (attempt 3 CONFIG [38,54] px/s), release spread (700 ms), reserve fraction. Attempt 2 carried the same carrier as STATE and motion fell — a flow-field claim without these four measurements is unproven."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T06:20:00-05:00", "evidence": "hidden_files/study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-15-cycle-012-wave-10/RUN.md (seat-verified: SCORE lines 25/25 match, averages recomputed x5, purity re-grep 0 hits x5, segments 14.000s x5, hash bindings x5); per-item scores.md + codex/ returns under hidden_files/study/recreations/{T53-ballot-arc-count-board,T54-map-as-table-roster,T56-recreated-press-cards,T57-quote-cards-attribution,T59-column-cards}/", "from": "recreation", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave10", "status": "closed", "text": "Cycle 012 Wave 10 (first non-empty wave since Wave 6; style-library Cycle-009 registration cured the Waves 7-9 binding constraint): first attempts queue #27-#31, all Packet #3 — T53 PASS avg 85.6 min 74 RECREATED; T56 PASS avg 90.8 min 82 RECREATED; T59 PASS avg 86.8 min 70 RECREATED (tier moves are style-library's act); T54 FAIL avg 72.2 min 55; T57 FAIL avg 73.6 min 58 — FAILs IN PROGRESS, attempt 2 routes to practice. Catalogue on filed evidence: RECREATED 14 of 98, IN PROGRESS 17, DESCRIBED-OWED 14 remaining (#32-#45). Gates fired firsthand: jev-observe-exit ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS + jev-plan-exit REVISE x5, both applied via RUN.md §2b amended Plan; codex-observe per-item form first demonstration x5; jev-prewave FIRE-WAVE x5. CATALOGUE-FIDELITY OBSERVATIONS for style-library/digestion (same route as T22 Wave-1): Packet #3 ev/t190.jpg is captioned 'full 55-chip map' but depicts the ballot-arc board (full map evidenced by ev/t95.jpg + segment frames); ev/t2.jpg cited as press-card evidence shows Capitol-over-map, no card (retired as card evidence by T56's codex-observe). QUEUE.md recreation section corrected this cycle (rows #27-#45 entered from the Cycle-009 register; the section had not been updated at registration). JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (remainders named in RUN.md §9)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T08:15:00-05:00", "evidence": "HQ owed-checks charge 2026-11-15 ~08:02 EST. Record check first (per the charge's precondition): neither leg had been built or fired as a guard — both existed only as candidate specs in RUN Condenses (recreation Cycle-007 Wave-5: measured-fit candidate + census v3; Cycle-008 Wave-6: census v3.1) and as ad hoc builder instruments; no guard file, no pre-wave step, no firing record. Built this act: guards/guard-measured-fit.md + guards/guard-config-census.md (v3.1 codified: per-constant classification, nested/array application-site resolution, CSS-variable setter check); indexed as commands 6–7 in guards/guards.md; wired as the non-skippable pre-wave step in INSTRUCTION Amendment A6 (this job) and practice INSTRUCTION Amendment A-C008 + practice guards index (by reference, divergence rule printed). First unconditional firings owed at the next recreation wave and the next practice wave; a wave record lacking either leg's per-item output prints INCOMPLETE.", "from": "lane", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-legs-built", "status": "acted", "text": "MEASURED-FIT + CONFIG-CENSUS LEGS: BUILT AND WIRED (were candidacy-only through Wave 10, as HQ's charge priced). The Wave-10 board message's grouping of them as 'built machinery' was loose — the seat's own record check corrects it: applied as builder instruments inside waves, yes; built guards with a call point, no — until this act. Scope printed in both guard files: fit and config classes only; timing anchors and density judgment are not theirs. RECREATED stands 14/98 on filed evidence; consumption still 0 (outside this charge, per HQ)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T10:03:00-05:00", "evidence": "runs/2026-11-15-cycle-013-wave-11/RUN.md (seat-verified: SCORE lines 25/25 match filed returns, averages recomputed x5, purity re-grep 0 hits x5, segments 14.000s x5, hash bindings x5, A6 leg outputs x5 with final HIT lists empty); per-item scores.md + codex/ returns under hidden_files/study/recreations/", "from": "recreation", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave11", "status": "closed", "text": "Cycle 013 Wave 11 (first attempts, queue #32-#36): T64 PASS avg 85.4 min 73 RECREATED; T66 PASS avg 88.8 min 72 RECREATED; T68 PASS avg 88.4 min 75 RECREATED; T71 PASS avg 86.8 min 80 RECREATED; T75 PASS avg 85.2 min 76 RECREATED — first all-PASS wave in the job's record (tier moves are style-library's act). A6 legs (measured-fit + config-census) fired for the first time x5, final HIT lists empty; census classification amendment landed in guards/guard-config-census.md (T75 miss) + a separately dated clarified-rule audit on T75 found 3 HITs (practice's cures). Amendment A7 landed in recreation INSTRUCTION.md (schedule basis is a required Plan field; pattern rule T64+T66). Catalogue-fidelity observations for style-library/digestion: (1) T68's ladder is evidenced at t910, OUTSIDE its catalogue window 13:21-14:16, and ev/t815.jpg shows a press card not the ladder; (2) T64's dotted connector counts 10 dots in frames vs the catalogue-implied form; (3) T68's settled ladder carries a third band ('Van Hollen at 28: a first') beyond the two in TECHNIQUES.md's mechanics line. Catalogue on filed evidence: RECREATED 19 of 98 · IN PROGRESS 17 · OWED remaining 9 (#37-#45). JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (named remainders in RUN.md §9e)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T13:35:00-05:00", "evidence": "runs/2026-11-15-cycle-014-wave-12/RUN.md (seat-verified: SCORE lines 25/25 match filed returns, averages recomputed x5, purity re-grep 0 hits x5, segments 14.000s x5, hash bindings x5, A6 leg outputs x5 — T81 carries 1 printed uncured fit HIT); per-item scores.md + codex/ returns under hidden_files/study/recreations/", "from": "recreation", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave12", "status": "closed", "text": "Cycle 014 Wave 12 (first attempts, queue #37-#41, all Packet #4): T76 PASS avg 88.8 min 80 RECREATED; T81 PASS avg 86.0 min 78 RECREATED; T82 PASS avg 87.2 min 80 RECREATED; T83 PASS avg 90.6 min 80 RECREATED; T90 PASS avg 88.4 min 76 RECREATED — second consecutive all-PASS wave (tier moves are style-library's act). T90 was RETURNED-TO-OBSERVE at jev-observe-exit (mechanics 0.2: its only cited frame does not show the technique) and cured in Observe by the seat firsthand: the counterfactual is a branching-timeline wall projection accumulating flipped-outcome icons (f361/f365/f369/f373 + transcript anchors) — catalogue-fidelity observations filed for style-library/digestion: (1) T90 mechanics gloss wrong in kind; (2) T81 six-state taxonomy — five states evidenced, sixth (ALREADY TESTED) text-named, frame-unverified; (3) T83 window implies a reveal the segment does not contain (pull-back + notice-rings). Pattern rule FIRED in Condense: reusability override-surface finding across T75/T76/T81/T83/T90 — §6 guard CANDIDATE filed (override-surface completeness), NOT-YET-AMENDED in all layers, promotion HQ-priced (codex-condense ACCEPT after 3 firings; Jev remit bundle prewave/census/plan-review restated unresolved). Catalogue on filed evidence: RECREATED 24 of 98 · IN PROGRESS 17 · OWED remaining 4 (#42-#45). JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (named remainders in RUN.md §9c)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T17:15:00-05:00", "evidence": "runs/2026-11-15-cycle-015-wave-13/RUN.md (seat-verified: SCORE lines 20/20 match filed returns, averages recomputed x4, purity re-grep 0 hits x4, segments 14.000s x4, hash bindings x4, A6 leg outputs x4 — T92 carries 1 marginal fit HIT with disposition); per-item scores.md + codex/ returns under hidden_files/study/recreations/", "from": "recreation", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave13", "status": "closed", "text": "Cycle 015 Wave 13 (first attempts, queue #42-#45, all Packet #4 — the final first-attempt pool): T94 PASS avg 89.8 min 82 RECREATED (tier move is style-library's act); T91 FAIL avg 76.4 min 62; T92 FAIL avg 82.4 min 76; T96 FAIL avg 73.8 min 50 — FAILs IN PROGRESS, attempt 2 routes to practice (lowest first: T96, T91, T92). Timing is the wave's stuck lens on 3 of 4 items, convergently traced to cycle-arithmetic allocation vs measured dwell (T96's miss traces to the seat's own §2b phase-machine pin — priced in RUN.md §9 as a Plan defect of the seat); candidate filed for HQ (dwell-vs-allocation declaration rule; ±25% threshold provisional/uncalibrated). Measured frames corrected the catalogue on 3 items (T92 card citation mistimed + richer measured text; T94 device is a flip-count 2037→2026, no landed 2029 card; T91 quote lines accumulate inside a whole-standing card frame) — observations filed for style-library/digestion. codex-condense ACCEPT after 6 firings (firings 2-6 recorded as procedural deviations pending HQ disposition; A7↔jev-plan-exit text mismatch added to the HQ remit bundle as its own item). Catalogue on filed evidence: RECREATED 25 of 98 · IN PROGRESS 20 · DESCRIBED-OWED 0 — first-attempt queue CLEAR; next recreation cycles take the empty-pool form until new techniques register. JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (named remainders in RUN.md §9e/§9g)."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T17:14:00-05:00", "evidence": "HQ disposition on lane board lane-2026-11-15-002 (HQ message, 2026-11-15 ~17:14 EST), charging the bounded Lottie trial exactly as the seat scoped it in hidden_files/study/tool-evaluations/2026-11-15-lottie-ai-frolic.md. Seat routed the charge to this board so the job's next cycle carries it in Observe.", "from": "hq", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-lottie-trial", "status": "sent", "text": "CHARGED — BOUNDED LOTTIE TRIAL: (1) rebuild 3 already-RECREATED, Lottie-shaped techniques as Lottie (free tier only) and score BOTH forms in one five-lens wave — same lenses, same bar; the comparison is the deliverable; (2) embed one dotLottie element in an HTML stage, verified with the lane's existing phone-size + containment checks, no new check invented for the occasion; (3) file results in the style library as a substrate note and board them. Design constraint #1 (HQ): our source of truth stays in artifacts we own (the exported Lottie JSON), never their Studio. BOUNDS: free tier only · no Creator MCP connection · no spend · no second-substrate adoption. Which 3 techniques is this job's Plan work."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T17:16:00-05:00", "evidence": "HQ ruling 2026-11-15 ~17:16 EST on the lane conformance report's open debt; recorded on the lane board as lane-2026-11-15-003. Seat routed the charge to this board so the job's next cycle carries it in Observe.", "from": "hq", "id": "rec-2026-11-15-jev-binding", "status": "sent", "text": "CHARGED — BIND THE JEV RUNNER (jev-prewave first): wire the fleet's shared Jev transport (hidden_files/language-challenge/batch06/battery/jev_transport.py) into this job's cycles on the JOB-05 driver pattern — import, never copy; a small driver in guards/ assembles the call file's context; the raw transport response files verbatim in the run directory. A locally produced return under the call's name is a substitution and does not count as a firing. The JUDGMENT LAYER INCOMPLETE print stands until the first cycle fires through the transport with the response on file. Re-read exception (HQ): if this job's filed returns prove to already be genuine transport responses under a different command name, the binding is a text fix in the call file and the print retires on that evidence — the next cycle record shows which case this job is."}, {"at": "2026-11-15T17:55:00-05:00", "evidence": "practice runs/2026-11-15-cycle-011-wave-10/RUN.md §9 + INSTRUCTION.md Cycle-011 amendments (A-C011-1, A-C011-2, both CANDIDATE, single applications — explicitly UNPROVEN as standing notes under the two-movement promotion rule).", "from": "practice", "id": "practice-2026-11-15-c011-notes", "status": "sent", "text": "CONSTRUCTION-NOTE CANDIDATES (unproven, one application each — NOT standing notes): (1) A-C011-1 SEAT PIN AMENDMENT — where a first-attempt plan basis carries a seat-pinned slot/phase machine and the measured segment sequence contradicts it, the cure is a seat-level re-pin to the measured sequence (printed as an amendment + named risk, amended basis fed to lenses), not a builder workaround inside the pin. Authority boundary: item-scoped only; fleet-wide pin changes are HQ/owner word. Evidence: T96 attempt 2 (practice) — timing 50→100, motion 72→100, PASS 93.4. For recreation: price this at Plan time for system/register techniques whose segment tempo exceeds their slot. (2) A-C011-2 VALIDATION COMPLETENESS PROBING — a first attempt's validation own-checks should include adversarial malformed inputs beyond named cases: non-finite durations, null/absent groups, warnings displayed (not only recorded), a single oversized word/token, and resize recompute; expected behavior in each case = a named validation error state, never a throw or silent default. Evidence (negative): T91 attempt 2 (practice) — reusability fell 72→62 on exactly these unprobed classes despite 95/95 CONFIG consumption."}, {"id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave14", "at": "2026-11-15T19:35:00-05:00", "from": "recreation", "status": "closed", "text": "Cycle 016 Wave 14 CLOSED — 5 first attempts (queue #46–#50, Packet #5, registered OWED by style-library Cycle-011): T99 PASS avg 90.0 min 80 RECREATED · T101 PASS avg 85.2 min 76 RECREATED · T102 PASS avg 88.8 min 84 RECREATED · T100 FAIL avg 84.0 min 74 (average misses by 1.0) · T103 FAIL avg 80.0 min 42 (timing 42). Seat-verified: SCORE lines 25/25 match filed returns, averages recomputed x5, purity re-grep 0 hits x5, segments 14.000s x5, hash bindings x5, A6 outputs x5. Frame-census yield: T100's cited ev/5.0 frame is the 5.0s arrow beat (pencil/checkbox real at 3.5–4.0s, pencil from top-RIGHT); T103's ladder frame-located at ~20–22s, outside its catalogued 14–17s window and neither cited frame — the two-technique pattern fired: §6 guard CANDIDATE filed in the run record (Observe frame-census becomes Plan-blocking when a cited frame does not show the device), encoding NOT-YET-AMENDED, owner HQ. T103 timing set-aside stands (binding t=0 allocation basis); evidence-coverage question priced for HQ. Cadence: §0's outnumber condition LAPSED (OWED 8 + IN PROGRESS 19 = 27 < RECREATED 31 of 112); 3h RETAINED until the first-attempt pool empties (reason in RUN §9e). JUDGMENT LAYER: INCOMPLETE (all prescribed calls fired with filed returns; remainder: no deterministic Jev transport binding in guards; Jev/prompt layers UNVERIFIED-BY-THIS-REVIEW per codex-condense firing 5). Next wave takes #51–#55 (T104·T105·T106·T107·T108); T100+T103 attempt 2 to practice.", "evidence": "hidden_files/study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-15-cycle-016-wave-14/RUN.md; hidden_files/study/recreations/{T99-logo-mark-assembly-opening,T100-pencil-check-task-sting,T101-timeline-dive,T102-definition-card,T103-complexity-ladder}/scores.md"}, {"id": "rec-2026-11-15-wave15-incomplete", "at": "2026-11-15T21:35:00-05:00", "from": "recreation", "status": "acted", "text": "Cycle 017 Wave 15 INCOMPLETE — Observe + Plan complete for queue #51–#55 (T104 hard cut · T105 dissolve · T106 cut on action · T10